      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T06:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that if the first capture group matches, there\u0027s a subtype, so you should actually discover for group(1) + \"._sub\" + group(2).\n\nFor example, _subtype._type._tcp --\u003e _subtype._sub._type._tcp\n\nSee: http://go/aocs/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/mdnsresponder/mDNSCore/DNSCommon.c;drc\u003d47e4cebad7397422144bb03a21f3f7682c062c4a;l\u003d699\n\nThis should be easy with:\n\n    final Pattern serviceTypePattern \u003d Pattern.compile(\"...regex\");\n    final Matcher matcher \u003d serviceTypePattern.matcher(serviceType);\n    if (!matcher.matches()) return null;\n    return matcher.group(1) \u003d\u003d null\n        ? serviceType + \".local\";\n        : matcher.group(1) + \"._sub\" + matcher.group(2) + \".local\";\n\n(which also replaces addLocalDomain).\n\nYou could put the actual discovery type as a member in MdnsListener, so you don\u0027t have to recalculate it in STOP_DISCOVERY (right now it calls addLocalDomain in both STOP_DISCOVERY and DISCOVER_SERVICES)",
      "revId": "8cf43509761e5e7e9c5c96b8f2bda95e236ebd00",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
